==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*friþuz}}, ultimately from {{der|ang|ine-pro|*preyH-||like, love}}. Cognates include {{cog|ofs|fretho}}, {{cog|osx|frithu}} ({{cog|nl|vrede}}), {{cog|goh|fridu}} ({{cog|de|Frieden}}), {{cog|non|friðr}} ({{cog|is|friður}}, Swedish and {{cog|da|fred}}). The Indo-European root is also the source of {{cog|grc|πρᾶος||mild}}, {{cog|sla-pro|*prijati}} ({{cog|cu|приꙗти}}, {{m|sla-pro|*prijateljь||friend}}), {{cog|cy|rhydd||free}} and {{cog|sq|praj}}, {{m|sq|Prenda}}.

